1
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:43,900
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,110 --> 00:01:46,890
[Episode 12]

3
00:01:48,229 --> 00:01:48,590
Okay.

4
00:01:56,310 --> 00:01:57,560
Why am I at your place?

5
00:01:57,759 --> 00:01:58,920
They all went home.

6
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:00,780
I have to take care of you, don't I?

7
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,560
I told Zhengguang

8
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:03,960
to pick you up after work.

9
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,590
Did I embarrass myself?

10
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:06,400
Yes.

11
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:13,360
Getting drunk
is a sign of respect for the alcohol,

12
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:14,030
right?

13
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:15,680
But

14
00:02:16,230 --> 00:02:18,710
it also depends on your constitution.

15
00:02:18,870 --> 00:02:20,800
You seem to lack that...

16
00:02:21,150 --> 00:02:22,750
What do experts call it?

17
00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:23,430
That...

18
00:02:23,430 --> 00:02:24,310
Acetaldehyde dehydrogenase

19
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:25,910
and alcohol dehydrogenase.

20
00:02:26,190 --> 00:02:27,000
What's that?

21
00:02:29,150 --> 00:02:30,310
It's some enzymes in everyone's body

22
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:32,630
needed to break down alcohol.

23
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:36,820
It basically means...

24
00:02:37,030 --> 00:02:39,690
You don't seem like someone
from the Northeast.

25
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:49,380
I'm not from the Northeast to begin with.

26
00:02:50,310 --> 00:02:51,310
Why do you have to be

27
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:52,840
so annoying when you speak?

28
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:06,750
If only I hadn't come over

29
00:03:06,750 --> 00:03:08,210
to eat noodles that night.

30
00:03:09,310 --> 00:03:12,510
There might still be a glimmer of hope
for resuscitation.

31
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:25,960
In all my years in the funeral business,

32
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,190
I've seen it all.

33
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,750
Who can say

34
00:03:29,750 --> 00:03:31,870
when someone will die or live?

35
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:34,840
Sometimes,

36
00:03:36,630 --> 00:03:37,750
the family notifies us,

37
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:39,190
saying the person has passed away,

38
00:03:39,190 --> 00:03:41,720
and we should hurry up
and make arrangements.

39
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:44,160
Then they suddenly catch their breath.

40
00:03:47,710 --> 00:03:48,430
Really.

41
00:03:50,710 --> 00:03:52,030
But there are also those

42
00:03:52,030 --> 00:03:53,120
who usually

43
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,520
look very healthy,

44
00:03:55,079 --> 00:03:56,740
with nothing wrong with them,

45
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:58,240
but suddenly,

46
00:04:00,630 --> 00:04:01,840
they're just gone.

47
00:04:08,910 --> 00:04:10,030
So before,

48
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:11,430
I also wondered about it.

49
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:14,390
But death doesn't discriminate by age.

50
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:16,480
You

51
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:19,820
treat the sick and save lives.

52
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:21,600
And I

53
00:04:22,950 --> 00:04:24,560
help those who can't be cured

54
00:04:25,190 --> 00:04:26,920
leave this world with dignity.

55
00:04:29,070 --> 00:04:30,720
We just do our best.

56
00:04:32,870 --> 00:04:35,360
As for when a person actually leaves,

57
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:38,510
that's for the King of Hell to figure out,

58
00:04:38,510 --> 00:04:39,270
right?

59
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:04,430
That hot and sour soup

60
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:05,950
is really good for a hangover.

61
00:05:05,950 --> 00:05:06,720
Is that so?

62
00:05:07,190 --> 00:05:08,560
I'm much more sober now.

63
00:05:09,830 --> 00:05:10,630
Thank you.

64
00:05:11,750 --> 00:05:13,680
Running away as soon as you wake up?

65
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:31,750
Jie.

66
00:05:34,310 --> 00:05:36,040
Is your probation period over?

67
00:05:37,270 --> 00:05:39,530
Do you want to become a regular employee?

68
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:41,510
I don't think I will.

69
00:05:41,510 --> 00:05:42,240
Why?

70
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,330
Do you look down on our work?

71
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:45,750
No, Jie.

72
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:47,460
I absolutely don't mean that.

73
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:50,950
Do you think you can just leave
whenever you want?

74
00:05:50,950 --> 00:05:52,240
What do you think

75
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:53,640
our Blossom & Fortune is?

76
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:58,800
What do you mean, Jie?

77
00:06:01,310 --> 00:06:02,950
We have to see you off.

78
00:06:04,950 --> 00:06:10,510
♪ Beyond the pavilion,
beside the ancient road ♪

79
00:06:10,510 --> 00:06:15,040
♪ Green grass stretches to the horizon ♪

80
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:20,720
♪ The evening breeze brushes the willows,
and the flute's notes fade away ♪

81
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:24,830
♪ The setting sun sinks
beyond range upon range of mountains ♪

82
00:06:24,830 --> 00:06:25,630
Stop!

83
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:27,970
Don't laugh.

84
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:31,950
Well.

85
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:36,190
Following an unreliable boss,

86
00:06:36,190 --> 00:06:37,430
I got infected a bit.

87
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:39,920
You're right.

88
00:06:40,270 --> 00:06:41,930
You really don't belong here.

89
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:44,360
You don't know how to

90
00:06:44,870 --> 00:06:46,470
find joy in sorrow like we do.

91
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:53,480
Your shop is quite big.

92
00:06:53,870 --> 00:06:55,330
Do you usually live alone?

93
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,830
I stay in the shop
on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays.

94
00:06:59,830 --> 00:07:03,090
I go home on Tuesdays, Thursdays,
Saturdays, and Sundays.

95
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,390
Such a big place.

96
00:07:05,390 --> 00:07:07,190
Aren't you scared living alone?

97
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:09,160
What's there to be scared of?

98
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,720
The ones you find scary

99
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:13,920
are the ones many people yearn for
day and night

100
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,630
but can never see.

101
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,680
Last time you came to the hospital
to see me,

102
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:24,480
you told me

103
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:26,390
you had that condition where you get dizzy

104
00:07:26,390 --> 00:07:27,190
when you read.

105
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:29,980
I was just kidding.

106
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:32,970
That's good.

107
00:07:42,159 --> 00:07:43,360
What's good about it?

108
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:48,760
It's always good to not be sick, right?

109
00:07:54,630 --> 00:07:56,630
If I really had that condition,

110
00:07:57,920 --> 00:07:59,120
could you cure me?

111
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:05,680
Yes!

112
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,070
My KTV career

113
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,190
is finally over!

114
00:08:09,950 --> 00:08:10,750
That's great!

115
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:20,800
[1314 Funeral Supplies,
Xiaoximen Store]

116
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:19,920
I'm leaving.

117
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:21,310
Get lost.

118
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:22,390
Sis.

119
00:08:22,750 --> 00:08:24,430
What time do you open tomorrow?

120
00:08:24,430 --> 00:08:25,720
I'll come over and help out.

121
00:08:25,210 --> 00:08:28,020
[1314 Funeral Supplies,
Xiaoximen Store]

122
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:27,070
Why are you coming?

123
00:08:27,070 --> 00:08:28,120
Didn't you quit?

124
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,390
I still feel that

125
00:08:30,390 --> 00:08:31,510
selling urns suits me.

126
00:08:31,510 --> 00:08:33,270
I was thinking of coming back
to continue working.

127
00:08:33,270 --> 00:08:34,270
Come on.

128
00:08:34,630 --> 00:08:35,270
You're past the age

129
00:08:35,270 --> 00:08:36,669
of selling urns.

130
00:08:36,870 --> 00:08:37,510
No.

131
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:39,960
Does selling urns have an age limit?

132
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:41,240
Sis, what are you talking about?

133
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:41,909
Besides,

134
00:08:42,270 --> 00:08:43,510
my previous performance

135
00:08:43,510 --> 00:08:44,480
was pretty good, wasn't it?

136
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:45,120
Yes.

137
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:46,120
But aren't you going

138
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,630
to Beijing to develop your career?

139
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:48,890
Our place is too small.

140
00:08:50,750 --> 00:08:51,550
Beijing...

141
00:08:51,670 --> 00:08:53,270
I haven't made up my mind yet.

142
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:55,130
What's wrong with you?

143
00:08:55,750 --> 00:08:57,210
You've become a stray dog?

144
00:08:57,870 --> 00:08:58,630
You don't know what to do,

145
00:08:58,630 --> 00:09:00,440
so you come to me
for a place to stay, right?

146
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:02,270
But if you admit you're a stray dog,

147
00:09:02,270 --> 00:09:03,530
I can let you come back.

148
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,520
But I don't think you are.

149
00:09:07,390 --> 00:09:08,200
See?

150
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:10,310
[1314 Funeral Supplies — at your service]

151
00:09:09,030 --> 00:09:10,490
Once this thing is posted,

152
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:11,910
many people come.

153
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:11,810
[Hiring]

154
00:09:11,910 --> 00:09:12,840
I have no choice.

155
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:13,550
This thing...

156
00:09:13,550 --> 00:09:14,790
One person per position.

157
00:09:14,790 --> 00:09:15,720
-Sis.
-So, look.

158
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:16,960
Now there's no position for you.

159
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:18,390
If you really love this industry,

160
00:09:18,390 --> 00:09:19,630
go check out other places.

161
00:09:19,630 --> 00:09:20,320
Sis.

162
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:23,210
[Funeral Wreaths and Burial Clothing]

163
00:09:20,510 --> 00:09:22,110
You're kidding, right, sis?

164
00:09:22,150 --> 00:09:23,080
Liu Zhengguang,

165
00:09:24,030 --> 00:09:25,290
are you leaving or not?

166
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:26,720
Sir, wait a moment.

167
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:27,870
I'm leaving, sis!

168
00:09:29,550 --> 00:09:30,390
Hurry up.

169
00:09:30,750 --> 00:09:31,550
Get in.

170
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:36,330
[Fucheng City Taxi]

171
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:47,720
Liu Zhengliang,

172
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:52,910
do you think I can find a job in Beijing?

173
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:54,960
How would I know?

174
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,870
If I don't go to Beijing,

175
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,390
what am I supposed to do here?

176
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:04,960
I don't know.

177
00:10:08,670 --> 00:10:10,510
Then tell me how I can

178
00:10:10,670 --> 00:10:13,200
cross the vast sea of suffering

179
00:10:13,270 --> 00:10:16,390
and reach the shore of enlightenment?

180
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:18,960
I want to know too.

181
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,480
Sir, what are you laughing at?

182
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:26,870
It's funny hearing you two young guys

183
00:10:26,870 --> 00:10:28,960
use such profound words.

184
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,390
Sir,

185
00:10:32,550 --> 00:10:33,270
driving a taxi,

186
00:10:33,270 --> 00:10:34,870
how much can you earn a month?

187
00:10:35,550 --> 00:10:37,480
Just enough to support the family.

188
00:10:37,790 --> 00:10:39,450
I don't eat big chunks of meat,

189
00:10:39,510 --> 00:10:40,630
and I can't wear brand-name clothes.

190
00:10:40,630 --> 00:10:42,030
It shouldn't be that bad, sir.

191
00:10:42,030 --> 00:10:43,150
The cost of living in Fucheng

192
00:10:43,150 --> 00:10:43,910
is so low.

193
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,750
The cost of living in Fucheng is low,

194
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:48,160
but my kid

195
00:10:48,190 --> 00:10:50,390
is studying at a university in Beijing.

196
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:53,270
What I earn alone

197
00:10:53,270 --> 00:10:54,930
is not enough for him to spend.

198
00:10:55,150 --> 00:10:56,150
Now,

199
00:10:56,510 --> 00:10:58,790
I just hope he graduates quickly

200
00:10:58,790 --> 00:10:59,960
and starts working.

201
00:11:00,870 --> 00:11:01,630
Every month,

202
00:11:01,630 --> 00:11:04,290
as long as he doesn't ask me for money,
it's fine.

203
00:11:04,790 --> 00:11:06,240
So is he staying in Beijing

204
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,360
or coming back?

205
00:11:07,910 --> 00:11:09,270
I asked him twice,

206
00:11:09,390 --> 00:11:10,080
but this brat

207
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:11,880
won't give me a straight answer.

208
00:11:12,390 --> 00:11:14,990
According to the saying
of our Fucheng people,

209
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,230
for an old horse that knows the way,

210
00:11:16,230 --> 00:11:17,290
the route is clear.

211
00:11:17,750 --> 00:11:20,010
Coming home and getting an iron rice bowl

212
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,650
is stable and respectable.

213
00:11:22,630 --> 00:11:25,000
A thousand-mile horse
that has high aspirations

214
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,840
will work hard in big cities
like Beijing, Shanghai,
Guangzhou, or Shenzhen.

215
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:29,170
What about a lost horse?

216
00:11:29,630 --> 00:11:30,790
Caught in a dilemma,

217
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,240
sighing in despair.

218
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:34,480
Today,

219
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,000
it's either dogs or horses.

220
00:11:37,510 --> 00:11:38,320
Sir,

221
00:11:38,630 --> 00:11:40,790
we are humans, not horses.

222
00:11:41,390 --> 00:11:42,480
Right, humans.

223
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:56,320
Sir, right here.

224
00:11:56,790 --> 00:11:57,600
Okay.

225
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,150
Bro,

226
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:01,170
remember what you said today.

227
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,840
No matter how things turn out,

228
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:04,770
you must treat yourself as a human.

229
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:06,650
Advice from me, Ma (horse).

230
00:12:07,750 --> 00:12:08,510
Seven yuan.

231
00:12:08,510 --> 00:12:09,600
Cash or QR code?

232
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:10,630
QR code.

233
00:12:15,870 --> 00:12:17,000
We're leaving, sir.

234
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:17,630
Goodbye.

235
00:12:27,390 --> 00:12:28,630
Hello, please change the dressing.

236
00:12:28,630 --> 00:12:29,540
Okay, I'll do it.

237
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:29,920
[Emergency Cart]

238
00:12:30,130 --> 00:12:34,200
[Emergency Cart]

239
00:12:32,870 --> 00:12:34,730
Where do you feel uncomfortable?

240
00:12:35,750 --> 00:12:37,030
I'm fifty-five.

241
00:12:38,270 --> 00:12:40,550
I used to be Chuizishan County's

242
00:12:40,550 --> 00:12:42,870
top turtle breeder.

243
00:12:47,790 --> 00:12:50,590
I'm proficient in Yin-Yang
and the Five Elements.

244
00:12:50,790 --> 00:12:52,590
I'm asking what your illness is!

245
00:12:53,550 --> 00:12:54,480
I'm not sick!

246
00:12:55,870 --> 00:12:56,550
Doctor,

247
00:12:56,550 --> 00:12:57,720
my dad often has

248
00:12:57,720 --> 00:12:58,550
epileptic seizures.

249
00:12:58,550 --> 00:12:59,390
When he has a seizure,

250
00:12:59,390 --> 00:13:00,630
his whole body twitches,

251
00:13:00,630 --> 00:13:01,630
and he foams at the mouth.

252
00:13:01,630 --> 00:13:02,910
How long have these symptoms lasted?

253
00:13:02,910 --> 00:13:04,200
For five or six days.

254
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:08,030
This is not an illness.

255
00:13:08,630 --> 00:13:10,670
It's an excess of Wood energy.

256
00:13:11,270 --> 00:13:13,800
Governing heavenly qi
is Taiyang Cold Water,

257
00:13:13,910 --> 00:13:16,200
guest Qi is Yangming Dry Metal.

258
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:23,200
Then

259
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,200
I'll take his blood pressure first.

260
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:25,120
Come, help him take off his clothes.

261
00:13:25,120 --> 00:13:25,600
Come.

262
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:28,790
-Sis.
-Yes?

263
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:30,600
Are there any small paper coffins left?

264
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:32,200
The ones at home are sold out.

265
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:33,720
There should be two small ones left.

266
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:35,270
Go check the loft bed.

267
00:13:35,270 --> 00:13:36,270
The loft bed, huh?

268
00:13:37,510 --> 00:13:39,170
These flowers are beautiful.

269
00:13:39,630 --> 00:13:41,440
Let's get some for our old shop.

270
00:13:41,870 --> 00:13:43,550
This is a different variety.

271
00:13:43,550 --> 00:13:44,120
Look.

272
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:45,440
Flowers like hydrangeas

273
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:46,670
and gentians,

274
00:13:47,030 --> 00:13:48,200
they look so nice for patients.

275
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,260
Arrange them a bit,

276
00:13:49,510 --> 00:13:50,960
and they'll be very pretty.

277
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:52,030
Our old shop

278
00:13:52,030 --> 00:13:54,510
only needs flowers suitable for funerals.

279
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:55,960
Wholesale is fine.

280
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,870
Who would go to a wreath shop

281
00:13:57,960 --> 00:13:59,560
to buy flowers for a patient?

282
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:00,870
Aren't they afraid of bad luck?

283
00:14:00,870 --> 00:14:02,360
Giving flowers
leaves a lingering fragrance.

284
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,690
How could it be bad luck?

285
00:14:03,870 --> 00:14:04,440
Come on.

286
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:07,080
If they think it's bad luck,
I won't sell to them.

287
